          "line": 154,
          "text": "    '. Strongest parsed root: state %d at %.3f eV with f(length)=%.5f; weakest: state %d at %.3f eV with f(length)=%.5f. '"
        },
        {
          "line": 155,
          "text": "    'The low-energy roots carry small dipole-length oscillator strength while the stronger roots at higher energy carry much '"
        },
        {
          "line": 156,
          "text": "    'larger values, so the low-energy and strong-transition regimes differ by computed transition intensity, not by any '"
        },
        {
          "line": 157,
          "text": "    'orbital-energy gap. These are vertical TDDFT response values at one fixed geometry, not experimental absorption maxima '"
